<title>GERMANY: German traders seek to export intervention rye.</title>
<headline>German traders seek to export intervention rye.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders sought to export just under 100,000 tonnes of intervention rye to third countries, state grain intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>An official could not give the precise tonnage at this time of day.</p>
<p>BLE received no other bids for intervention grain exports at this week's EU cereals export tender.</p>
<p>--Hanover newsroom, +49-511-36598-11</p>
</text>
